  "text": "That sounds like a wonderful idea! A classic breakfast omelette is a comforting and delicious way to show your mom how much you care. Here's a simple and reliable recipe for a classic breakfast omelette that's sure to impress:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf73 Classic Breakfast Omelette Recipe\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 3 large eggs\n- 1/4 cup milk or cream (optional, for fluffiness)\n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n- 1/4 teaspoon black pepper\n- 1/4 teaspoon paprika or chili powder (optional, for a bit of kick)\n- 1/4 cup shredded cheese (cheddar, mozzarella, or your favorite)\n- 1/4 cup cooked and chopped vegetables (bell peppers, onions, spinach, mushrooms, etc.) \u2013 optional\n- 1/4 cup cooked bacon or sausage \u2013 optional (for added flavor)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. **Whisk the Eggs:** In a bowl, beat the eggs with the milk or cream, salt, pepper, and any spices (like paprika or chili powder) you'd like to add. Let the mixture rest for a few minutes.\n\n2. **Heat the Pan:** Heat a non-stick skillet or frying pan over medium heat. Add a small amount of oil or butter.\n\n3. **Cook the Egg Mixture:** Pour the egg mixture into the pan. Let it set around the edges, but don\u2019t let it fully solidify in the center yet.\n\n4. **Add Fillings:** If using cheese, vegetables, or meat, add them to the center of the omelette once the edges are just starting to set.\n\n5. **Fold the Omelette:** Use a spatula to carefully fold the omelette in half. Cook for another 1\u20132 minutes, or until the cheese is melted and the omelette is fully cooked through.\n\n6. **Serve:** Flip the omelette (if desired) or slide it onto a plate. Serve warm, optionally with toast, fruit, or a side of yogurt or hash browns.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf81 Tips for a Special Mother's Day Breakfast:\n\n- **Keep it Personal:** Add a note or a small gift to go with the breakfast.\n- **Make it Fancy:** Use a pretty plate or add a decorative napkin.\n- **Include Her Favorites:** Find out what foods she loves and include them.\n- **Take a Photo:** Capture the moment and send it to her with a heartfelt message.\n\n---\n\nI hope your mom enjoys your breakfast in bed! It's a thoughtful and delicious way to celebrate her. Let me know if you'd like a version with specific ingredients or dietary restrictions! \ud83c\udf73\u2764\ufe0f",
